      "message": "I don\u0027t feel strongly about this, but I would also remove this.  Two arguments:\n\n* If we remove, then when it is actually needed in a later CL, the readers/reviewers can see how this is plumbed/introduced.\n* But maybe more importantly: It is unclear if this will be needed because:\n    - `image` crate handles this internally today.  I guess we may need to expose this for streaming rows one-by-one.  But then if we do, then `bottomUp` will come from the `image` crate, so we probably should remove for now the `bottom_up` calculations in `experimental/rust_bmp/ffi/FFI.rs`\n    - I am not 100% clear on how scanline-vs-incremental decoding approach needs this.  If incremental always wants a top-down decoding + if we decide to reuse `blink::SkiaImageDecoderBase` as-is, then we probably won\u0027t need to know if the image is bottom-up or top-down (because \"incremental\" may force us to fully decode bottom-up inputs and then proceed without actual/real streaming).",
